Show the non-sensitive version, commit, and build date linked into this binary.

INPUTS
  No positional input. --json selects the stable machine envelope.

OUTPUT
  Build identity in human text or as data in the JSON envelope.

ERRORS
  Output failures return INTERNAL with exit code 10.

Usage:
  moment version [flags]

Examples:
moment version --json

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for version

Global Flags:
      --as string                     local account username for content operations; not accepted in API mode
      --data-dir string               local Moment data directory (direct mode)
      --json                          write one machine-readable JSON document to stdout
      --log-format string             stderr log format: text or json (default "text")
      --log-level string              stderr log level: error, warn, info, or debug (default "info")
      --no-input                      fail instead of prompting for input
      --reauth-password-file string   private file containing the current password for sensitive API operations
      --timeout duration              maximum command duration (default 30s)
      --token-file string             file containing an account API token
      --url string                    Moment HTTP API base URL (API mode)
